{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"predicate logic predicate logic","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md","fileName":"Predicate Logic.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Predicate Logic","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Formal Logic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Formal Logic","Propositional Logic","Universal Quantifier","Existential Quantifier","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"predicate logic predicate logic","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md","fileName":"Predicate Logic.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Predicate Logic","heading":"Predicate Logic","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Predicate logic extends [[Propositional Logic]] by representing properties and relations that become propositions when applied to entities. A one-place predicate P associates each entity in its domain of discourse with the proposition P(a), while predicates with several places express relations among several entities.\n\nVariables in an open statement remain free until a [[Universal Quantifier]] or [[Existential Quantifier]] binds them. This lets logic express general claims that propositional variables alone cannot preserve.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Formal Logic","Propositional Logic","Universal Quantifier","Existential Quantifier","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Predicate Logic.md","sourceType":"markdown","section